.TH "MINIOS\-LIVE" "1" "October 2025" "MiniOS Live System Builder" ""
.SH NAME
minios\-live \- step\-by\-step build tool for creating bootable MiniOS
ISO images
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]minios\-live\f[R] [\f[I]start_cmd\f[R]] \f[B]\-\f[R]
[\f[I]end_cmd\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]minios\-live\f[R] is a step\-by\-step build tool that builds
bootable MiniOS ISO images.
It uses pre\-defined configurations to create a customized MiniOS live
system with a controlled and modular build process, including the
ability to add software layered on top of the base system using SquashFS
modules.
.SS Build Options
Using \f[B]minios\-live\f[R], you can build various configurations
including:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Debian distributions:\f[R] Buster (10), Bullseye (11), Bookworm
(12), Trixie (13)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Ubuntu distributions:\f[R] Jammy (22.04), Noble (24.04)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Desktop environments:\f[R]
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Debian:\f[R] Xfce (standard), Flux (minimum), LXQt (Bookworm/Trixie
only)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Ubuntu:\f[R] Xfce only
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Package variants:\f[R]
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]All Debian:\f[R] Standard (xfce), Minimum (flux)
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Bookworm/Trixie only:\f[R] Toolbox, Ultra
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Ubuntu:\f[R] Standard only
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Architectures:\f[R] amd64, i386 (for older distributions)
.SS Prerequisites
.IP \[bu] 2
It is advisable to use the latest version of Debian or Ubuntu for
building.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]WARNING\f[R]: Never run scripts from the \f[B]linux\-live\f[R]
folder directly.
It will break your system.
.SH COMMANDS
\f[B]minios\-live\f[R] breaks down the build process into discrete
steps:
.TP
\f[B]build\-bootstrap\f[R]
Installs a minimal base system using \f[B]debootstrap\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]build\-chroot\f[R]
Installs the remaining core components and chosen desktop environment
within the chroot environment
.TP
\f[B]build\-live\f[R]
Creates the main SquashFS image containing the core MiniOS system
.TP
\f[B]build\-modules\f[R]
Builds additional SquashFS modules containing extra software packages
.TP
\f[B]build\-boot\f[R]
Copies the boot files, generates the initrd and the necessary boot
configuration files
.TP
\f[B]build\-config\f[R]
Generates configuration files for the build
.TP
\f[B]build\-iso\f[R]
Creates the final ISO image, incorporating both the core SquashFS image
and any additional modules
.TP
\f[B]remove\-sources\f[R]
Removes source files after the build
.SH USAGE
.TP
\f[B]start_cmd\f[R]
(Optional) The build stage to start from.
If omitted, starts from the first command
.TP
\f[B]\-\f[R]
(Optional) A range operator for running command sequences
.TP
\f[B]end_cmd\f[R]
(Optional) The build stage to end with.
If omitted, ends with the last command
.SS How it works
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]No arguments (./minios\-live)\f[R]: Displays help information
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Single command\f[R]: Runs only that specific command
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]start_cmd \- end_cmd\f[R]: Runs all commands from start_cmd to
end_cmd
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\- end_cmd\f[R]: Runs from the beginning up to end_cmd
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]start_cmd \-\f[R]: Runs from start_cmd to completion
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\- only\f[R]: Runs the entire build process from start to finish
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the build from start to finish:
.IP
.EX
minios\-live \-
.EE
.PP
Start the build by building the base environment and finish by
installing the entire system in chroot:
.IP
.EX
minios\-live build\-bootstrap \- build\-chroot
.EE
.PP
Start the build from the beginning and finish by installing the entire
system in chroot:
.IP
.EX
minios\-live \- build\-chroot
.EE
.PP
Start the build by building the base environment and run to completion:
.IP
.EX
minios\-live build\-bootstrap \-
.EE
.PP
Build only ISO image from previously prepared data:
.IP
.EX
minios\-live build\-iso
.EE
.SH CONFIGURATION
Edit the configuration file \f[B]/etc/minios\-live/build.conf\f[R] to
specify your preferred distribution, desktop environment, and additional
software to be included in the SquashFS modules.
Alternatively, use \f[B]minios\-cmd\f[R](1) for an easier configuration
experience.
.PP
This modular approach allows for greater flexibility and maintainability
when customizing your MiniOS live system.
You can easily add or update software by modifying the SquashFS module
configurations and rebuilding only the affected modules using the
appropriate \f[B]minios\-live\f[R] command.
